.TH PDP1CONTROL 1 "November 2026" "pidp1-mods" "PiDP-1 Commands"
.SH NAME
pdp1control \- start, stop and configure the PDP-1 simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY pdp1control
.BI start " [switches]"
.YS
.SY pdp1control
.BI "stop | restart | reload | status"
.YS
.SY pdp1control
.BI "set " interface
.YS
.SY pdp1control
.BI "panel " frontpanel
.YS
.SY pdp1control
.BI "usbtape | t30dpy | soroban " y/n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdp1control
owns the life cycle of the
.BR pdp1 (1)
emulator and the programs around it.
It starts the front panel driver (real PiDP-1 hardware or the on-screen
virtual panel), the emulator in a detached
.BR screen (1)
session, the chosen user interface, and feeds the emulator the boot
configuration that matches the sense switch setting.
.PP
The start-time choices are kept per user in
.IR ~/.config/pidp1-mods/pdp1control.config ,
as name=value lines; the commands below write it, and
.BR pdp1central (1)
edits the same file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " [switches]"
Start everything.
.I switches
is the boot selector number, normally read from the front panel sense
switches with
.BR scanpf (1);
it selects
.IR /var/lib/pidp1-mods/bootcfg/ n .cfg,
whose
.B PDP1_DIR
token names the tape library.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the emulator, the panel drivers and the interface programs.
.TP
.B restart
.B stop
followed by
.BR start .
.TP
.B reload
Re-read
.IR /etc/pidp1-mods/pidp1.config
(SIGINT to the emulator).
.TP
.B reloadt30
Re-read the Type 30 display configuration (SIGHUP to
.BR t30dpy (1)).
.TP
.BI set " interface"
Choose the user interface:
.BR gui " (pdp1_periphES windows), " web " (the pdpsrv browser front end) or " apps " (standalone programs such as t30dpy)."
.TP
.BI panel " frontpanel"
Choose the front panel:
.B pidp
for the PiDP-1 hardware,
.B virtual
for the on-screen panel.
.TP
.BI usbtape " y/n"
Use USB sticks as the paper tape reader and punch.
.TP
.BI t30dpy " y/n"
Start the Type 30 display along with the simulator.
.TP
.BI soroban " y/n"
Start the Soroban typewriter terminal along with the simulator.
.TP
.B status
Report what is running.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PIDP1_ENV
Where to find the locations file
.IR pidp1-env.sh ;
by default the one beside this script.
Setting any of
.BR PIDP1_STATEDIR ,
.BR PIDP1_DATADIR ,
.BR PIDP1_LIBEXECDIR ,
.B PIDP1_BINDIR
redirects that part of the install, which is how a build tree or a test
root is used without editing anything.
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/pidp1-mods/pdp1control.config
per-user start-time choices
.TP
/etc/pidp1-mods/pidp1.config
site configuration for the emulator and the panel drivers
.TP
/var/lib/pidp1-mods/bootcfg
the per-selector boot configurations
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pdp1 (1),
.BR pdp1central (1),
.BR pdp1ctl (1),
.BR t30dpy (1)
